.SH NAME
cgcalc \- a double precision calculator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cgcalc
.RB [ \-analog ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B CGCalc
is a double precision calculator application. It provides advanced
scientific and mathematical features such as trigonometric functions
(sine, cosine, tangent) and logarithms (log, ln).
.PP
Most buttons have a key as well: the digits, operators and parentheses
are typed as themselves, Return or = gives the result, BackSpace takes
back the last digit, Delete clears the entry and Escape clears
everything. On the scientific keypad, the letters on the function
buttons (s, c, t, l, r, e, p, i, d) press them. Edit \(-> Copy puts
the result in the clipboard.
.SS Programmer mode
View \(-> Programmer changes to a keypad for whole numbers: words of
8, 16, 32 or 64 bits, shown in hexadecimal, decimal, octal or binary,
and signed (two's complement) or unsigned, as SGN is down or up.
Arithmetic wraps round within the word. AND, OR, XOR, NOT, MOD and the
shifts (<< and >>) are there, taken in C's order of precedence; >>
shifts a signed word arithmetically, and division truncates as C's
does. Every bit of the word is shown beneath the display, and clicking
one flips it.
.PP
The letters a to f type the hex digits, and &, |, ^, ~, %, < and >
press AND, OR, XOR, NOT, MOD, << and >>. F5, F6, F7 and F8 choose
hexadecimal, decimal, octal and binary, and F12, F2, F3 and F4 a word of
64, 32, 16 and 8 bits. Edit \(-> Copy writes a word as C would, with
0x, 0 or 0b before it.
.PP
Changing keypads carries the number shown and the memory across, cut to
a whole word on the way to the programmer's; a calculation left
unfinished is dropped.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-analog
Run as a slide rule instead, as the X11R3
.BR xcalc (1)
did. On the slide, button 1 puts its left index under the pointer,
button 2 drags it and button 3 puts its right index under the pointer.
Elsewhere, button 1 moves the hairline, button 2 makes the rule twice
as long and button 3 half as long again. Shift with button 2 or 3
quits.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a summary of the options and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.PP
The usual GTK options, such as
.BR \-\-display ,
are also understood.
